-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  Version 0.1.0 (2026-11-06)
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  * Initial release (ORDER 252c, study item J19): KDE Connect's ufw application profile is allowed once from the
    private and link-local network ranges (RFC 1918, RFC 3927; with IPv6 on, RFC 4193 and RFC 4291 2.5.6), as ordinary
    ufw rules, when ufw and the profile are both on the system. The firewall stays off by default, as Debian ships it.
    A dpkg trigger on /etc/ufw/applications.d runs it, so the order of the installs does not matter. A profile handled
    once is recorded, so a rule the person deletes in System Settings, Firewall stays deleted. A rule that cannot be
    added is said and kept by sparky-stereo-problems with a repair. The message is in the nine languages.
